  "id": "maculele",
  "name": "Maculelê (Santo Amaro stick dance)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Afro-Brazilian stick-fighting dance of Santo Amaro da Purificação in the Bahian Recôncavo, revived in the mid-twentieth century by Paulino Aluísio de Andrade (Popó do Maculelê) and since spread across Brazil through capoeira groups. Dancers in a ring strike pairs of wooden sticks (grimas) against their own and their partners' on the accented beats, to songs led by a soloist and answered in chorus over atabaques and agogô. Palitos stand in for the grimas and the source-unspecified agogô for the bell.",
